name: sim.packDoubleTable
description: Packs ab array of double floating-point numbers into a string
luaSynopsis: bytes data = sim.packDoubleTable(list doubleNumbers, int startDoubleIndex = 0, int doubleCount = 0)
pythonSynopsis: buffer data = sim.packDoubleTable(float[] doubleNumbers, int startDoubleIndex = 0, int doubleCount = 0)
inputs:
1. doubleNumbers: array of double floating-point numbers. Non-numbers will be packed as zero values
2. startDoubleIndex: zero-based index from which on data should be packed. Can be omitted in which case 0 is used
3. doubleCount: amount of doubles that should be packed. Can be omitted in which case 0 is used (which indicates that the maximum available doubles should be packed from the indicated startDoubleIndex)
outputs:
1. data: a buffer (values between 0 and 255) that contains packed double floating-point numbers
